## Incident Classification

### Severity Levels

| Severity | Description | Examples |
|----------|-------------|----------|
| P1 - Critical | Active breach, data exfiltration, widespread impact | Ransomware, confirmed breach, major outage |
| P2 - High | Potential breach, significant risk | Suspicious access, vulnerability exploitation |
| P3 - Medium | Security event requiring investigation | Malware detection, policy violation |
| P4 - Low | Minor events, informational | Failed login attempts, spam |

### Classification Criteria

| Factor | P1 | P2 | P3 | P4 |
|--------|----|----|----|----|
| Data Exposure | Confirmed PHI/PII | Potential | Limited | None |
| System Impact | Production down | Degraded | Single system | None |
| Customer Impact | Multiple customers | Single large | Single small | None |
| Regulatory | Breach notification likely | Possible | Unlikely | No |
| Reputation | Media attention likely | Possible | Unlikely | No |

